  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Addressing Water Vulnerability in the Caribbean SIDS</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The initiative targets enhancing the resilience of water systems in Caribbean Small Island Developing States (SIDS) by assessing climate change impacts, improving data collection for water resources, and promoting information sharing among stakeholders. It prioritizes identifying adaptation and mitigation measures for water vulnerability by addressing climate impacts on water ecosystems, enhancing data availability through better monitoring platforms, and facilitating the sharing of best practices. Additionally, a significant focus is placed on collaborating with specific Caribbean SIDS to update maps of transboundary aquifers and groundwater systems, leveraging their potential for climate change adaptation.</narrative>
  </description>
